Release milestone: API freeze, docs, SemVer, PyPI. Owner decisions 2026-10-16:
- Complete rebrand to `openpptx`: distribution, import package and repo (`RorySullivan1/openpptx`). The
  PyPI name `pypptx` belongs to an unrelated 2015 project.
- No users yet, so nothing renamed before 1.0.0 gets a deprecation shim.
- The contract is the documented surface (oxml/opc/parts are internal, not renamed).
- Docs on GitHub Pages; the LICENSE carries python-pptx's notice.

Detail is in the card, `.meta/roadmap/stages/04-stable-release/v1.0.0.md`.

## Goals
- Ship as `openpptx`: renamed distribution and import package, full metadata, root LICENSE with
  python-pptx's notice.
- Public API contract: audit the API layer, stability and deprecation page (in force from 1.0.0),
  public-name snapshot test.
- Docs: guides per area, migration guide from python-pptx, CHANGELOG back to v0.1.0, Pages deploy.
- Release pipeline: Trusted Publishing on a `v*` tag; `1.0.0rc1` first, then `1.0.0`.

## Objectives / acceptance
- [ ] CI green on 7 cells (suite, corpus, examples, work-count gate); coverage ≥ the branch-start baseline.
- [ ] `sphinx-build -W -E` clean; Pages serves the reference, guides, stability page and migration guide.
- [ ] sdist and wheel `openpptx` carry LICENSE with both notices; `twine check` passes; the built wheel runs
      every example on 3.9 and 3.13.
- [ ] The public-API snapshot test passes.
- [ ] PowerPoint 16 opens every example's output without repair.
- [ ] `pip install openpptx==1.0.0rc1` works from PyPI (owner-run); migration guide reviewed (human-gated).
